{
  "$schema": "../vector.schema.json",
  "format": "webway-vectors/v0",
  "kind": "blob/verify",
  "description": "What a fetcher has after one reply stream. Input {\"hash\", \"size\" (from the reply), \"ranges\" (the reply's ranges), \"data\": {\"pattern\": n}, \"mutate\"?: {\"flip\": byte offset} | {\"truncate\": length} | {\"append\": hex}, \"end\"?: \"fin\" (default: the provider closed the stream) | \"reset\" (stream reset or connection lost)}. The stream is the honest encoding of data for ranges, then mutate applied to it. Output {\"verified\": blocks kept, \"missing\": blocks of ranges not verified, \"complete\": every block of ranges verified, \"failure\": null | \"BlobCorrupt\" | \"ProtocolError\"}. BlobCorrupt: data did not match. ProtocolError: bytes after the end, or a clean FIN before it. A reset before the end is not a failure: the rest is fetched again.",
  "spec": "ext/blob.md#54-verification",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "whole",
      "description": "Whole blob",
      "requirements": [
        "BLOB-021"
      ],
      "input": {
        "hash": "blake3:d93c23eedaf165a7e0be908ba86f1a7a520d568d2d13cde787c8580c5c72cc54",
        "size": 100000,
        "ranges": [
          [
            0,
            7
          ]
        ],
        "data": {
          "pattern": 100000
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "result": "accept",
        "output": {
          "verified": [
            [
              0,
              7
            ]
          ],
          "missing": [],
          "complete": true,
          "failure": null
        }
      }
    },
